{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits","id":1555716,"title":"What makes Maeljin different from just powerful vice spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-21T05:50:28-08:00","id":1555716,"title":"What makes Maeljin different from just powerful vice spirits?","content":"Your average spirit is already evil and insane by human standards anyways. So how can Maeljin be even <i>worse</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T07:11:38-08:00","id":1555723,"title":"","content":"<i>World of Darkness: Inferno</i> goes over this a bit: ordinary spirits of Vice are still part of an interconnected symbolic ecosystem that feeds into the wider world, but the direction of the Maeljin and their servants is to make the world worse on purpose \u2014 werewolves' usual justification of their drives notwithstanding the Shadow is actually pretty good at balancing itself out in the long run even if the result isn't necessarily ideal for humans, but the Maeltinet push things toward poisoning the world toward self-destructive behavior and engendering an underlying lack of respect for the world.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, the spirits of the Wounds are evil by human standards in a way that is meaningful within the context of what normal spirits are \u2014 a normal spirit only understands things through the lens of its portfolio (see that bit in the Idigam Chronicle Fiction Anthology where an Ithaeur realizes that a death-spirit being fond of him is actually part of the reason it's trying to kill him), but a Diabolus has some level of empathy and flexibility of thought that makes its sowing of corruption and disaster a meaningfully evil choice.<br /> <br /> It may likewise be worth noting that the Maeljin themselves are so distant that it's repeatedly emphasized that not all of the different names for them might refer to separate entities (up to and including &quot;every named Maeljin is a mask for the same being&quot;) and that Wounded spirits are stated or directly implied in multiple cases to be less immortal than normal spirits by dint of the Wounds generally being one-way trips for anything that hasn't been turned into a demon. Wounds are holes in the world \u2014in Inferno's terms, their atrocious resonance serves as the base conditions for opening a gateway to Hell, and in Mage's terms, the Inferno is part of the Lower Depths, realms that are missing something essential for existence, such that usually the only things that can come out of them are the &quot;natural&quot; denizens (or things so corrupted as to be denizens themselves).<br /> <br /> tl;dr The Maeljin and their servants aim to make the world materially worse in a way that is selfish beyond the monomania of ordinary spirits because of an intersection of &quot;fuck you, got mine&quot; and being literally empowered by disaster, corruption, negativity and atrocity; they're literally not a part of the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Grammar fixes. 11-21-2025, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T12:09:06-08:00","id":1555731,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Right, so Maeljin are like an oilspill or nuclear radiation for the spirit world, right?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T12:23:49-08:00","id":1555732,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27062_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27062\" data-vbnamecard=\"27062\">VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</a> That's more what Wounds are.<br /> <br /> I don't think we ever actually get a straight answer as to what the Maeljin are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T13:14:52-08:00","id":1555735,"title":"","content":"If you need a metaphor, noting that there are limits to what metaphor can do:<br /> Think of Wounds literally. Wounds are vulnerable to <i>infection.</i> The Maeljin are the outside agents whose influence slips into the Wound to cause the infection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T14:34:15-08:00","id":1555742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits?p=1555731#post1555731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Right, so Maeljin are like an oilspill or nuclear radiation for the spirit world, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Maeljin&quot; are the set of names to which the Maeltinet, the Bale Hounds, and (nominally) Soulless Wolf claim allegiance. If they exist in a more concrete capacity than that, it is as extradimensional invaders looking to make awful beachheads into the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The things you've mentioned are impersonal \u2014 the agents of the Maeljin are actively and willfully attempting to poison and undermine the Shadow like a conspiracy of sadists and saboteurs, with the big names themselves being the gods that they worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T19:00:19-08:00","id":1555780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits#post1555716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your average spirit is already evil and insane by human standards anyways. So how can Maeljin be even <i>worse</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>On top of everything else, appreciating that the Shadow doesn't entirely work off of human standards can help. Humanity can stand on its doorstep and call everything that passes by evil, that doesn't make it so. The Maeljin are not fundamentally impacted by anything humanity thinks of them or it, and the word &quot;evil&quot; never appears near their section in Shunned by the Moon. They're aspects of corruption and subversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-22-2025, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T13:32:02-08:00","id":1555805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits#post1555716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your average spirit is already <b>evil </b>and <b>insane </b>by human standards anyways. So how can Maeljin be even <i>worse</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>By human standards the <i>average </i>spirit would not be evil, it would be monomaniatic, hyper-focused, and not at all really complex intellectually to be called evil.<br /> <br /> Average spirits would be on the weaker side, so no higher mental functionality; average spirits would be a reflection of a single concept, and only caring for that, e.g. squirrel-spirits would not think convoluted squirrel world domination plans or concentration camps for the other species, they just want squirrel-resonance. They get squirrel-resonance from squirrels, and things related to squirrel-kind. Same would go for trolley cart spirits, blanket spirits, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maeljin on the other hand, are a combination of spirits feeding from what we humans call evil as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> has rightly put, plus the fact their home ground (the Wounds), is literally an anti-natural thing for the Shadow and the world at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-23-2025, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T12:46:21-08:00","id":1555890,"title":"","content":"Am I right to think that even in Second Edition, Werewolf presents spirits that possess or claim people as tending to use them to do some kind of fucked up stuff (beyond the very act of doing that to people in the first place)?<br /> <br /> Still, I'm imagining that manages to be distinct from Wound spirits if those have a tendency to do things that are deliberately atrocious, even to other spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T13:54:47-08:00","id":1555891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits?p=1555890#post1555890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right to think that even in Second Edition, Werewolf presents spirits that possess or claim people as tending to use them to do some kind of fucked up stuff (beyond the very act of doing that to people in the first place)?<br /> <br /> Still, I'm imagining that manages to be distinct from Wound spirits if those have a tendency to do things that are deliberately atrocious, even to other spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits possess and claim people to do things that their natures impel them to do, most conventionally to propagate the resonance that empowers them and/or as part of political maneuvers in the spirit courts; often times this is at least without regard for their victims' lives and relationships, but while there are doubtless bits of the spiritual framework rites are built on that rely on transgressive or atrocious acts those are particular instances rather than the default.<br /> <br /> In broad terms, Ridden and Claimed are the Storm Lords' favored prey because possession et al is easier to foist upon the weak and/or weakened and, going way back to 1e, spirits as a horror element represent consequences and many spirits reflect the weakness and selfishness of human action or the failings of werewolves \u2014 the roiling ecosystem of the Shadow is a thing to keep on top of, particularly to the Storm Lords' view of the hunt as an ancestral duty, and the balancing act of getting one's territory under control is because individual spirits tend not to know when to stop expanding without external pressures.<br /> <br /> Wounded spirits's activities are more in the vein of how the Strix will steal bodies to do fucked up shit on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Added missing word and corrected typo. 11-26-2025, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T15:01:20-08:00","id":1556070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits?p=1555890#post1555890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right to think that even in Second Edition, Werewolf presents spirits that possess or claim people as tending to use them to do some kind of fucked up stuff (beyond the very act of doing that to people in the first place)?<br /> <br /> Still, I'm imagining that manages to be distinct from Wound spirits if those have a tendency to do things that are deliberately atrocious, even to other spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part it seems to be more of an act of survival. Their food source is diminished, they're being edged out by other predators, or something bigger than them is taking over and these spirits have decided it's worth risking the terrors of the flesh to survive, and basically being considered outcasts from spirit 'society,' which they might have been already.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's usually rarer that they are part of some sort of stars aligning plot to summon Gozer or Wepwawet or whomever.<br /> <br /> Outside of Wounded spirits, or spirits of sadism or cruelty, spirits themselves don't claim out any sense of atrociousness or desire for cruelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-01-2025, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T21:24:37-08:00","id":1556082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits?p=1556070#post1556070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of Wounded spirits, or spirits of sadism or cruelty, spirits themselves don't claim out any sense of atrociousness or desire for cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even spirits of sadism or cruelty don't in terms we would call &quot;conscious&quot;, or &quot;deliberate&quot;.<br /> <br /> Normal spirits act out of survival and instinct. Whatever they are and do, at the end of the day they're moved by the vagaries of Shadow ecology, be it escaping predators or trying to increase access to their &quot;food&quot;. Spirits of bad things will represent them, but ultimately their actions are explained out of the same things as any other spirit, it's all Shadow ecology running as it should.<br /> <br /> Wound spirits are purposefully evil. They differ from other spirits first and foremost that they developed the capacity to desire things beyond their natural scope, an awareness of other beings as actors with their own desires and interests, and from this they <u><b>chose</b></u> to harm people for fun. So, while the spirit of pain and cruelty seeks to spread pain and cruelty because it will produce Essence they can eat, the spirit from a Wound will actually go out of its way and may abdicate of opportunities to feed or grow, sometimes even risk their safety, just because they <b>want</b> to do evil for evil's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T01:31:30-08:00","id":1556088,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Where are you getting that from? What you're saying is familiar, but I can't find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T07:53:48-08:00","id":1556096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555716-what-makes-maeljin-different-from-just-powerful-vice-spirits?p=1556088#post1556088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Where are you getting that from? What you're saying is familiar, but I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 60 of Inferno, in the &quot;Abilities&quot; section describing how Diaboli differ from normal ghosts and spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T08:23:25-08:00","id":1556126,"title":"","content":"I feel like the differences b/w woun